4. Three Audit Tasks for FL-02 Through FL-04
Task 1: Research Paper Analysis
Audit task: Use AI to help me analyze research papers related to Machine Learning, NLP, and fake review detection.
“Done well” means:
•	The research problem, methodology, dataset, models, and evaluation metrics are correctly identified. 
•	At least 3 key contributions and 2 limitations/research gaps are identified. 
•	Technical concepts are explained clearly in my own words. 
•	Important claims are checked against the original paper. 
•	I can explain the paper’s main idea and findings without relying on AI’s wording. 
Success measure: I can produce a structured analysis of a paper and explain its methodology and findings independently.

Task 2: Python/ML Code Debugging
Audit task: Use AI to diagnose and fix errors in my Python and Machine Learning projects.
“Done well” means:
•	The exact error and its root cause are identified. 
•	AI explains why the error occurred before suggesting a fix. 
•	The proposed solution works in my actual development environment. 
•	The fix does not unnecessarily break existing functionality. 
•	I test the corrected code successfully. 
•	I understand the solution well enough to explain it myself. 
Success measure: The code runs successfully after debugging, and I can explain both the problem and the solution.

Task 3: Academic and Technical Writing Improvement
Audit task: Use AI to improve the clarity, structure, grammar, and technical quality of my research papers, thesis sections, and project documentation.
“Done well” means:
•	The original meaning and technical claims are preserved. 
•	Grammar, sentence structure, and clarity are improved. 
•	The writing has a logical flow and appropriate academic tone. 
•	No fabricated information or citations are introduced. 
•	Technical terminology is used correctly. 
•	I review and verify the final version before using it. 
Success measure: The revised version is clearer and more concise than the original while remaining factually accurate and consistent with my actual research.

